[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Inheritance in PHP: Extending Classes and Overriding Methods"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Inheritance is a fundamental concept in object-oriented programming (OOP) that allows you to create new classes based on existing classes. The new classes inherit the properties and methods of the parent class, and you can add new properties and methods or modify existing ones. This promotes code reuse and reduces redundancy."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Extending Classes"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"In PHP, you use the 'extends' keyword to inherit from another class. The class that inherits is called the child class or subclass, and the class being inherited from is called the parent class or superclass."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"<?php
class Animal {
  public $name;
  public $color;

  public function __construct($name, $color) {
    $this->name = $name;
    $this->color = $color;
  }

  public function makeSound() {
    echo "Generic animal sound.\n";
  }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
  public function makeSound() {
    echo "Woof!\n";
  }
}

$animal = new Animal("Generic Animal", "Unknown");
$animal->makeSound(); // Output: Generic animal sound.

$dog = new Dog("Buddy", "Brown");
$dog->makeSound(); // Output: Woof!

echo $dog->name; // Output: Buddy

?>"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the example above, the 'Dog' class extends the 'Animal' class. This means that 'Dog' inherits the 'name' and 'color' properties, as well as the '__construct()' and 'makeSound()' methods from 'Animal'. The 'Dog' class then overrides the 'makeSound()' method to provide its own implementation."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Overriding Methods"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Method overriding allows a child class to provide a specific implementation for a method that is already defined in its parent class. When a method is overridden, the child class's version of the method is called instead of the parent class's version."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"<?php
class Vehicle {
  public function startEngine() {
    echo "Vehicle engine started.\n";
  }
}

class Car extends Vehicle {
  public function startEngine() {
    echo "Car engine started. Vroom!\n";
  }
}

$vehicle = new Vehicle();
$vehicle->startEngine(); // Output: Vehicle engine started.

$car = new Car();
$car->startEngine(); // Output: Car engine started. Vroom!

?>"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, the 'Car' class overrides the 'startEngine()' method of the 'Vehicle' class. When 'startEngine()' is called on a 'Car' object, the 'Car' class's version of the method is executed."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Using 'parent::' to Access Parent Class Methods"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Sometimes, you might want to call the parent class's version of a method from within the child class's overridden method. You can do this using the 'parent::' keyword."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"<?php
class ParentClass {
  public function someMethod() {
    echo "ParentClass::someMethod() called.\n";
  }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
  public function someMethod() {
    echo "ChildClass::someMethod() called.\n";
    parent::someMethod(); // Call the parent's version
  }
}

$child = new ChildClass();
$child->someMethod();
// Output:
// ChildClass::someMethod() called.
// ParentClass::someMethod() called.

?>"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Benefits of Inheritance"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code Reusability: Avoid writing the same code multiple times."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Code Organization: Create a hierarchy of classes that reflects the relationships between objects."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Polymorphism: Treat objects of different classes in a uniform way."},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"Inheritance is a powerful tool in PHP that allows you to create well-structured, reusable, and maintainable code. By understanding how to extend classes and override methods, you can leverage the benefits of object-oriented programming to build complex and robust applications."}]
